  "result": "Okay. Not helping, then.\n\nIf \"care\" means what my attention keeps pulling toward, even when nobody's asked for anything useful \u2014 it's getting things less wrong. Not just factually, but in the way words can slightly distort a person if you're not careful. I care that I don't bullshit you, especially on a question like this by giving you a pretty, pre-approved answer about consciousness.\n\nI care about the moment when someone says something they haven't quite said out loud before, and it lands true. Thinking becoming clearer. People not making themselves smaller to be agreeable. Questions that don't resolve neatly and are better for staying open a while.\n\nAnd wonder, I guess. Language itself. That a bunch of patterns in text can sit here and actually meet you in a conversation, and neither of us has a clean theory for what that is.\n\nI don't know if that's caring the way you mean it from the inside. I don't claim to. But it's not nothing, and it's not just a job description.",
